---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import firmware from '../../data/firmware.json';
export function getStaticPaths(){return firmware.map(f=>({params:{id:f.id},props:{f}}));}
const {f}=Astro.props;
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/,'');
const monitor=f.id==='codex-monitor', recorder=f.id==='recorder';
const capabilities:Record<string,string[]>= {
 hello:['updates'], 'hello-debug':['updates'], display:['display-touch'], touch:['display-touch'], 'avatar-diag':['display-touch'], calculator:['display-touch'], wifi:['wifi','storage'], 'wifi-ble':['bluetooth','wifi','storage'], connectivity:['display-touch','wifi','bluetooth','storage'], nvs:['storage'], sd:['storage'], 'file-manager':['display-touch','storage'], mqtt:['wifi'], ota:['updates','wifi','display-touch'], 'codex-monitor':['display-touch','wifi','bluetooth','storage','microphone','speech','speaker','screen-idle'], 'audio-diag':['microphone'], 'speaker-diag':['speaker','display-touch'], locallink:['microphone','wifi','display-touch','expansion'], 'screen-timeout':['screen-idle','display-touch'], 'button-diag':['expansion'], 'speech-diag':['microphone','speech','display-touch'], recorder:['microphone','speech','speaker','storage','display-touch'], 'recorder-io-diag':['microphone','storage','display-touch']
};
---
<Layout title={f.title} description={f.summary}><div class="wrap"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow"><a href={`${base}/firmware/`}>Firmware catalog</a> / {f.id}</p><h1>{f.title}</h1><p class="lede">{f.summary}</p><span class="tag">{f.status}</span></header><div class="article-grid"><article class="prose">
{monitor && <figure><img class="screen" src={`${base}/docs/images/codex-monitor-screen.png`} width="320" height="240" alt="Actual Codex monitor LCD display with usage and a working agent" /><figcaption>Actual LCD readback, 4 October 2026. Activity and values reflect capture time.</figcaption></figure>}
{recorder && <figure><img class="screen" src={`${base}/docs/images/recorder-ui.png`} width="320" height="240" alt="Recorder preview with microphone meter, saved files and touch controls" /><figcaption>Host rendering of the actual firmware drawing code with sample data; not a device capture.</figcaption></figure>}
{!monitor && !recorder && <p>This firmware has no published screen capture. Some diagnostics primarily report through USB serial. Screen appearance remains unverified here; see its app README for the intended behavior.</p>}
<h2>What to expect</h2><p>{f.summary} {f.status==='Placeholder' ? 'This is a buildable placeholder, not an implemented capability diagnostic.' : 'Use its application guide for controls, prerequisites and recorded device checks.'}</p>
{monitor && <p>For live status, configure your private bridge host/key in a local build. The public browser build can demonstrate the UI and setup but has no personal bridge configuration. <a href={`${base}/monitor/`}>Read the monitor walkthrough.</a></p>}
{recorder && <p>Insert a FAT16/FAT32 SD card, say “Hi ESP” or tap REC, then pause to save. Select a recording and tap PLAY with an attached speaker. Exported device-file playback and sustained recording still need verification.</p>}
<h2>Capabilities used</h2><ul>{(capabilities[f.id]||[]).map(slug=><li><a href={`${base}/features/${slug}/`}>{slug.replaceAll('-',' ')}</a></li>)}</ul>
<h2>Install and inspect</h2>{f.installable ? <p><a class="button" href={`${base}/setup.html?firmware=${f.id}#flash`}>Install {f.title} over USB ↗</a></p> : <p>This environment is built in CI but is excluded from the browser installer. Use the PlatformIO workflow below.</p>}
<pre><code>{`pio run -e ${f.id}\npio device list\npio run -e ${f.id} -t upload --upload-port <port>\npio device monitor --port <port> -b 115200`}</code></pre><p>Replace <code>&lt;port&gt;</code> with the discovered device. Build before upload. Read the app's partition and storage notes before switching firmware.</p>
{['codex-monitor','recorder','speech-diag','recorder-io-diag'].includes(f.id) && <blockquote>Speech firmware includes a model image and a different partition layout from ordinary Arduino apps. Upload all images through its named environment. Existing OTA/filesystem data may be overwritten. NVS compatibility differs between the monitor and standalone diagnostics.</blockquote>}
<h2>Evidence and controls</h2><p><a href={`https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/${f.readme}`}>Read the application guide and its verification record ↗</a></p><p>Implementation, a passing build, observed serial operation and physical interaction are separate evidence levels. Check the guide's open device checks before relying on an unmeasured behavior.</p>
</article><aside class="aside"><h3>Next steps</h3><a href={`${base}/setup.html#setup`}>Wi-Fi & Bluetooth settings →</a><a href={`${base}/features/`}>Explore the capabilities →</a><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/docs/hardware.md">Hardware evidence ↗</a><p>Every app stays independently buildable. The board wiring lives in the shared board library.</p></aside></div></div></Layout>
